% Goal-level checks are per goal, and the constructor-arity walk is one
% of them: a goal that applies a declared constructor at the wrong
% arity is rejected before the query runs, exactly as a rule body would
% be. `ok_pair` pins that the right arity still goes through.
:- module(tgc, [store/1, type(pair/0)]).

:- chr_type pair ---> pair(int, int).

:- chr_constraint store(pair).

keep @ store(_) <=> true.
